# Project agent routing

Read root [AGENTS.md](../AGENTS.md), the changed package's README, native manifests/locks and deeper AGENTS first.
Select procedures for the actual task, not every installed skill. Shared methods/resources live in `agent-skills`;
this directory owns only project routing and setup. It is not a skill/plugin installation directory.

- Common's SDD/TDD, selective DDD, source-first and design references apply when that task needs them; no copied manual
  or mandatory layer/interface is required. Keep actual project contracts in `docs/specs` and decision rationale in `docs/adr`.
- Use behavioral regression for changed behavior, characterization for preservation and static checks for prose.
  Run actual owning-package gates. Examples never add dependencies or override local policy, authority or safety.
- Use built-in host agents by default. Claude-native packaged agents and explicit Codex custom-agent exports differ;
  Codex plugins do not load custom-agent TOMLs in the verified clients.

